<title>USA: Rust Int'l to sell scaffolding business.</title>
<headline>Rust Int'l to sell scaffolding business.</headline>
<dateline>OAK BROOK, Ill. 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>WMX Technologies Inc said Wednesday its majority owned subsidiary, Rust International Inc, has agreed to sell its scaffolding business for about $190 million to DLJ Merchant Banking Partners LP and Carlisle Enterprises LP.  </p>
<p>The sale of Rust scaffolding business is expected to close in the third quarter of 1996, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>WMX said the transaction is part of its ongoing program to monetize non-core assets and investments.</p>
<p>WMX provides environmental services.</p>
<p>	     Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787</p>
